        "agreement_type": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Primary classification of each financial agreement. Equity financing: investor takes an ownership stake in the project in exchange for capital. Debt financing: Capital provided as a loan to the developer, repaid with interest over time. Offtake agreement: A contract committing a buyer to purchase a defined volume of carbon credits from a project at a set (or formula-based) price once the credits are issued. Forward purchase: A buyer pays upfront (or in tranches) for credits to be delivered in the future. Revenue share: investor receives a percentage of the project's credit sale proceeds in exchange for capital or services, rather than fixed repayment or equity. Grant: Non-repayable funding provided by a donor, government, or philanthropic body, usually tied to eligibility criteria or reporting obligations but not to financial returns. Guarantee: a commitment by a third party (e.g., insurer) to cover losses or obligations if the project fails to perform.",
